  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A first name, Muslim or Christian in its Burkinabè spelling (Inoussa, Rasmané, Salamata, Bibata, or Jean-Baptiste and Pélagie), and a family name from the father. Mossi family names like Ouédraogo, Sawadogo and Kaboré are the most common in Ouagadougou. Mossi first names often carry Wend (God): Wendkouni (gift of God), Wendyam. Dioula and Bobo families of the west carry names like Ouattara, Traoré and Sanou, Fulani families Diallo and Dicko, and Gourmantché families Ouoba and Lompo. Joking kinship (rakiiré) links whole communities, so Mossi and Samo, or Bobo and Peul, tease each other when they meet.",
